==English==

===Etymology===
US criminal underworld slang, 1906 (noun), 1915 (verb), thinning alteration of {{m|en|graft}}.<ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary}}</ref><ref>''A Dictionary of the Underworld: British and American'', Eric Partridge (2015), [https://books.google.com/books?id=MUbeCQAAQBAJ&pg=PA307&dq=grift p. 307]</ref><ref>''Word Origins...And How We Know Them: Etymology for Everyone'', Anatoly Liberman (2009), [https://books.google.com/books?id=sMiRc-JFIfMC&pg=PA32&dq=grift p. 32]</ref> The lighter sound (‘a’ → ‘i’, /ɑː/ or /æ/ → /ɪ/) is associated with more subtle, sophisticated crime; compare {{m|en|swindle}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɡɹɪft/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɪft|lang=en}}

